{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider","id":1089921,"title":"New Sidereal Homebrew for 3e: Down Came the Spider","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-08T13:26:45-07:00","id":1089921,"title":"New Sidereal Homebrew for 3e: Down Came the Spider","content":"Greetings!<br /> <br /> While there are already two different Sidereal Homebrews for Third Edition, I personally could not honestly give my recommendation to either. Grifftofer's Sidereals has gone without updates or a sign of life for around a year, while Where Fate Has Led has some tremendous problems with trying to reinvent the wheel, and loses some of the charms, effects and other neat mechanical concepts that made Sidereals come alive for me. So, rather than trying to take the bits I like from both and cobbling together something, I decided to take a few of my NPC Sidereal charms I've made over time and make them usable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NhOn8TrzeGXr0llm2CZOYcbHpBSGTyXebei79IIjfRY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NhOn8TrzeGXr0llm2CZOYcbHpBSGTyXebei79IIjfRY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NhOn8TrzeGXr0llm2CZOYcbHpBSGTyXebei79IIjfRY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NhOn8TrzeGXr0llm2CZOYcbHpBSGTyXebei79IIjfRY/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Current goals are to create a version of Sidereals that fits within the mechanics of Third Edition, while retaining the theme and general charm effects of previous editions. While most charms in first and second edition will be making a reappearance, some new charms will be added to fill in the gaps, boosting the average length of a charm tree from 5-6 charms to 12-15. Rework Paradox into an effect that shows a Sidereal's impact on Creation, and provides a mechanic for the Fate Glitches they are sent to fix. Give Ronin an actual feel to them. Give Craft: Fate an actual purpose outside of planning committees.<br /> <br /> Current Status: Character Creation is finished, every single charm tree has at least 3 essence 1 charms. Should be barebones, but enough for a playtest. In the middle of updating College Information","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":11713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","user":"ZX_XZ","date":".  I hit enter twice and it posted before I finished. 05-08-2017, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T13:32:54-07:00","id":1089928,"title":"","content":"Reserved for Future Updates","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T13:48:03-07:00","id":1089936,"title":"","content":"Downloading! Although I have not played First or Second edition, I love sidereals, although I have not convinced my players to play a sidereal campaign (or to make one of them ST one :P). Will read and give my opinion, although I can\u00b4t say a lot, as I have not experience with them in any other edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T13:58:42-07:00","id":1089943,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Glad to see we have some interests. This is far from done, so check out for updates. Still not 100% certain if I'm going to keep resplendancies as they are, or turn them into charms. On one hand, its another thing to track which causes problems, but on the other hand its nice to have access to these Mini charms no matter what, especially Provable Location of the Gate. I may end up folding the most powerful and useful of them into Anima effects to be honest","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:31:46-07:00","id":1089963,"title":"","content":"Now it\u00b4s good to ask something about Resplendent Destinies which I have always wanted to know:<br /> <br /> Do they change the sidereal shape/form/appearance, or it is just a &quot;Now, you don\u00b4t recognize me&quot;? When I have put sidereals NPCs into the game, I have used the first option, just not to have the meta thing of &quot;Oh, geez, we met a bald, green eyed man with a broken nose. Again. With the same face that the merchant, the monk and the bounty hunter had, I wonder who he is!&quot;, but I assume it is the second one, Clark Kent style XD<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:45:49-07:00","id":1089975,"title":"","content":"You don't change appearance, and that can cause problems. If someone met you in a Resplendant Destiny and they meet you in a different Resplendant Destiny and they recognize you, Paradox is generated because as far as the Universe is concerned, you're not the same person but that guy sees through the ruse. Now, in previous Editions, Sidereals got +3 dice to any roll to hide or disguise themself because of Arcane Fate and could disguise themselves as their Resplednant Destiny with no penalties, and any mortal opposing that roll lost 3 dice. So its a good idea to have a disguise associated with each destiny. I'm going to put in a e1 larceny charm that will let you make your disguise attempt instantly if you do it concurrently with putting on a Resplendant Destiny now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:50:50-07:00","id":1089978,"title":"","content":"Eh, that\u00b4s cool. You see? As I have not played sidereals in any other edition, and in fact, the only non-3e book I have is &quot;Games of Divinity&quot;, I can\u00b4t really help you with feedback. But will try to test it with my players when I can!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the information. As I I have only used a sidereal NPC in my games, and has been changing appearance, and he is a bit of a sorcerer, I will probably go with &quot;No, they don\u00b4t change appearance, but he has a custom spell/hearthstone/artifact which allows him to do it&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:22:16-07:00","id":1090076,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone! I have a new potential update I wanted to get feedback upon. Currently I was planning on giving each College two Resplendency powers, but the system felt clunky. So, an Idea I had was to give each caste 3 of their best Resplendency powers as part of their anima banner. Here is the first draft:<br /> <br /> <b>Anima Banner Powers</b><ul><li>For 1 mote, Sidereals may determine the exact time of date through sensing the position of the stars. Incidentally, this also tells the Sidereal how much Paradox is in the area</li> <li>For 1 mote, Sidereals may display a Caste Mark upon their forehead</li> <li>The Sidereal may spend 1 mote to learn of any portals to Yu-Shan or Malfeas within long range. She knows not where they are, she only learns of their presence.</li> <li>For 3 motes, the Sidereal may burn a letter written on fine silk, addressed to another Sidereal. The Letter appears on that Sidereal's skin and buzzes to alert him of its presence</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Journeys</b><ul><li>For 16m, the Sidereal makes the Lesser Sign of Mercury, adding her (Essence) dice to all ally's rolls to rush or Disengage for the rest of the Scene. Every level of anima above Dim reduces the cost of this ability by 5m</li> <li>Poetic Sacrifice Insurance: For 3m, the Sidereal may ignore penalties by terrain or bad weather, and ignores nonmagical difficult terrain</li> <li>Field Mouse Rider: The Sidereal may ride any familiar without causing it harm or facing any difficulty of her own. If the Speed bonus of the mount is below (Essence) it instead becomes (Essence)</li> <li>Good Worker Spirit: For 4m per day, no one will believe the Sidereal is slacking, no matter how little work she does. This is an Illusion effect. The Bureau of Destiny has persistent problems with Sidereals using this on the job.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Serenities</b><ul><li>For 16m, the Sidereal makes the Lesser Sign of Venus, adding her (Essence) dice to all ally's rolls to instill or inspire positive emotions. Every level of anima above Dim reduces the cost of this ability by 5m</li> <li>Proper Plumage: The Sidereal is always considered well dressed and fashionable, no matter what her attire actually is. Even the scent of sweat and horse dung will be recieved as a perfume</li> <li>Handsome Boy Eyes: For 4m, the Sidereal may make seduction attempts with only a glance, needing no supporting intimacy</li> <li>Comforting Matriarch Embrace: The Sidereal may hold and comfort someone, before putting them to sleep and paying 5m. If she does so, the target will have a rest uninterupted by nightmares and recovers an additional willpower</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Battles</b><ul><li>For 16m, the Sidereal makes the Lesser Sign of Mars, adding her (Essence) to all ally's Soak. Every level of anima above Dim reduces the cost of this ability by 5m</li> <li>Weak Spine Sense: The Sidereal always known whether anyone has an intimacy of fear towards her, and if so how intense it is</li> <li>Several Arrows of Reason: After landing an attack against a Creature outside of fate, the Sidereal may pay 4m to ignore all natural soak and (Essence) hardness. If the attack deals even a single point of damage, the Creature is considered inside Fate for the rest of the scene</li> <li>Wounded Lion Strength: By paying 1wp, the Sidereal may add her wound penalty to the damage of her next decisive attack</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Secrets</b><ul><li>For 16m, the Sidereal makes the Lesser Sign of Jupiter, adding her (Essence) dice to all ally's rolls to Read intentions, and (Essence/2) to their Guile. Every level of anima above Dim reduces the cost of this ability by 5m</li> <li>Stab the Seer's Eyes: The Sidereal is aware of any astrological reading to detect her, and may pay 3m to change or distort the reading</li> <li>Talisman Making Touch: For 1wp, the Sidereal may bless a small object and give it to someone in need. The object becomes a Talisman with Resources value equal to the Sidereal's Essence</li> <li>Provable Location of the Gate: For 20m, 2wp, the Sidereal may prove that the Calibration Gate will appear here and within 5 minutes, it is so. Stepping through the Gate returns her and her allies to Yu-Shan, and it dissapears as soon as all of her friends step through</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Endings</b><ul><li>For 16m, the Sidereal makes the Lesser Sign of Saturn, adding her (Essence) damage to all ally's damage rolls. Every level of anima above Dim reduces the cost of this ability by 5m</li> <li>Reading Dead Eyes: After eating a Corpse's eye, and spending 2m, the Sidereal learns of the last thing the Corpse saw before it died and whether the body left behind a ghost or hungry ghost</li> <li>Harvest Ripe Wheat, Falling Feather Hay: The Sidereal instantly knows how corrupt an organization is as soon as she steps within its confines. This tells her nothing about individual members, just the organization as a whole</li> <li>Tears of the Blade: Once per scene. the Sidereal makes the Sign of the Sword at a mortal and pays 10m, 2wp. The mortal either dies immediately of heart attack, or dies in a horrific fashion of the Sidereal's design within 5 days. In combat, this costs an additional 15 initiative. After using this ability, the area's paradox immediately rises by 2.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":11713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","user":"ZX_XZ","date":".  cleaner markup 05-08-2017, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:55:26-07:00","id":1090087,"title":"","content":"While I (obviously <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) disagree about Where Fate Has Led, I'm always interested in seeing other Sidereal ideas that I can plunder from <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T19:00:55-07:00","id":1090088,"title":"","content":"Lol, we've had our disagreements in the past but I will say despite our different ideas about the direction Sidereals should take, you have done really good work in the past and I'm glad to hear that you'll be looking at my work","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:25:41-07:00","id":1090143,"title":"","content":"Im curious about your choices of abilities and what informed them. For example I would have thought now martial arts are freed up from caste abilities that Melee would be a more obvious choice for Endings over Brawl. The executioners Sword over the pugilists fists? Also there is a lot of overlay between the caste abilities of Secrets and Endings Awareness, Integrity, Occult, Stealth. Why does Endings have Integrity? Thas seems to be about maintaining, resisting change, enduring keeping intimacies. this seems to run counter to the message of Endings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:02:53-07:00","id":1090210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider?p=1089978#post1089978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the information. As I I have only used a sidereal NPC in my games, and has been changing appearance, and he is a bit of a sorcerer, I will probably go with &quot;No, they don\u00b4t change appearance, but he has a custom spell/hearthstone/artifact which allows him to do it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Previous editions had a Terrestrial spell called &quot;Disguise of the New Face&quot; that allowed just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:43:09-07:00","id":1090232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider?p=1090210#post1090210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Previous editions had a Terrestrial spell called &quot;Disguise of the New Face&quot; that allowed just that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. I already talked to the &quot;sorcerer&quot; player (not a sorcerer, just a Night Caste who is starting to learn sorcery) and as he would be interested into learning it, we had decided to make it a ritual, able to turn you into a generic person with the specified characteristics (&quot;Black skinned fourty years old woman&quot; or &quot;Blond skinny teenager boy&quot;), but with the capacity of being used like &quot;Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares&quot;, so, if you have a personal item or a body part of the person you want to turn into, you can adopt his/her shape. If it is your control spell, you also adopt his/her mannerisms and speech style, making you very difficult to detect unless you act grossly out of character.<br /> <br /> How does it work in previous editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T05:07:33-07:00","id":1090242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider?p=1090232#post1090232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting. I already talked to the &quot;sorcerer&quot; player (not a sorcerer, just a Night Caste who is starting to learn sorcery) and as he would be interested into learning it, we had decided to make it a ritual, able to turn you into a generic person with the specified characteristics (&quot;Black skinned fourty years old woman&quot; or &quot;Blond skinny teenager boy&quot;), but with the capacity of being used like &quot;Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares&quot;, so, if you have a personal item or a body part of the person you want to turn into, you can adopt his/her shape. If it is your control spell, you also adopt his/her mannerisms and speech style, making you very difficult to detect unless you act grossly out of character.<br /> <br /> How does it work in previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>It took 10 mins to cast, had you roll Int+Larceny or Int+Craft(Fate) to create a disguise according to normal rules (including supplementing the roll with Charms), but the spell supplied the disguise and let you change your mannerisms, Appearance score and even anima display.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T19:32:37-07:00","id":1090559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermes12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider?p=1090143#post1090143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im curious about your choices of abilities and what informed them. For example I would have thought now martial arts are freed up from caste abilities that Melee would be a more obvious choice for Endings over Brawl. The executioners Sword over the pugilists fists? Also there is a lot of overlay between the caste abilities of Secrets and Endings Awareness, Integrity, Occult, Stealth. Why does Endings have Integrity? Thas seems to be about maintaining, resisting change, enduring keeping intimacies. this seems to run counter to the message of Endings?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason behind a few of these choices is due to the abilities in First and Second Edition and the discrepencies between them. In First edition, Endings had Martial Arts, Athletics, Bureaucracy, Medicine and Awareness. In the Transition to Second edition, Endurance stopped being an ability as it was far too close to resistance. They were combined, and given to Journeys who previously had Endurance. Brawl was removed, and its place in Battles was exchanged for War. Athletics was given to Battles to fill in the gap, and Integrity was given to Endings because Endings needed an additional ability. I've given Brawl to Endings because of its link to Martial Arts in this Edition, and kept Integrity in Endings as a reference to its location in Second Edition while shuffling a few things around. I agree that Secrets and Endings as of right now are too close together, so my current proposal is<ul><li>Secrets: Lore, Occult, Investigation, Larceny, Stealth, Socialize, Integrity</li> <li>Endings: Medicine, Brawl, Athletics, Integrity, Awareness, Bureaucracy, Stealth</li> </ul><br /> This lowers the amount they share to two abilities (Stealth and Integrity) and gives a bit more credibility to Endings Castes as Heaven's assassins. Awareness I had originally given to Secrets because I thought the future sight charms would fit, and Integrity helps you from spilling the beans. With this arrangement, Secrets keeps Integrity and also gains Socialize, an excellent ability for keeping secrets and discerning the secrets of others.<br /> <br /> Any opinions over the proposed caste ability changes and Anima ability first drafts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T02:18:47-07:00","id":1091027,"title":"","content":"I always thought there were some weird allocation. in my mind you have 5 archetypes. The Intrepid Messenger, The Consummate Socialite, the Tactical general, the Secret agent and the Implacable assassin<br /> <br /> Journeys: Ride, Sail, Athletics, Survival, Dodge, Archery, Brawl<br /> Serenity: Bureaucracy, Socialize, performance, Craft, Linguistics, Occult, Presence<br /> War: Presence, Melee, Archery, Resistance, Lore, Ride<br /> Secrets: Stealth, Larceny , Investigation, awareness, integrity, Lore, Occult<br /> Assassin: Medicine, Stealth, Resistance, Dodge, Thrown, Melee, athletics<br /> <br /> They are pretty radical re thinks but I think they create 5 really distinct classes of Sidereals that really feel like they have the skills related to their fields. Obviously they all have access to martial arts anyway so Serenity and Secrets not having a combat affiliation is hardly crippling in a combat scenario plus they are also both sorcerous now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T17:30:33-07:00","id":1091348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermes12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider?p=1091027#post1091027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought there were some weird allocation. in my mind you have 5 archetypes. The Intrepid Messenger, The Consummate Socialite, the Tactical general, the Secret agent and the Implacable assassin<br /> <br /> Journeys: Ride, Sail, Athletics, Survival, Dodge, Archery, Brawl<br /> Serenity: Bureaucracy, Socialize, performance, Craft, Linguistics, Occult, Presence<br /> War: Presence, Melee, Archery, Resistance, Lore, Ride<br /> Secrets: Stealth, Larceny , Investigation, awareness, integrity, Lore, Occult<br /> Assassin: Medicine, Stealth, Resistance, Dodge, Thrown, Melee, athletics<br /> <br /> They are pretty radical re thinks but I think they create 5 really distinct classes of Sidereals that really feel like they have the skills related to their fields. Obviously they all have access to martial arts anyway so Serenity and Secrets not having a combat affiliation is hardly crippling in a combat scenario plus they are also both sorcerous now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly fond of that large a departure from the original caste abilities.<br /> <br /> Updated the Anima effects and added to the Doc. Finished Thrown! Now with 12 charms, all based on throwing things at people and making them really unhappy with the current situation. Any requests for the next ability I should do or effects you would like to see?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T16:16:59-07:00","id":1096894,"title":"","content":"Since last time I updated, added a ton of new stuff<br /> <br /> EDIT: I've added a ton of e2 and 3 charms, expanded most lists e1 repetoires as well. Character creation is finished, Astrology is mostly done","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":11713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","user":"ZX_XZ","date":". 05-25-2017, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T09:44:57-07:00","id":1097168,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4m liking the shape of this, and find pretty cool the version of Paradox you are using (or going to use, at least, as there is little info about it). I am digging this, and I think will use it for my sidereal NPCs (or even PCs! I can maybe get to convince the other GM to use a Sidereal NPC, and as our games have an irregular schedule, I doubt I will lack content before I need it XD)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T12:24:16-07:00","id":1097215,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Really glad to hear that there is interest in this project, it really helps keep me going. I'll be expanding paradox with a sorta scale with examples soon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":11713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","user":"ZX_XZ","date":". 05-26-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T21:29:27-07:00","id":1099387,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, update time! I have finished Brawl, Occult and have sprinkled e2 and e3 charms among all the other trees. Please Evaluate and Comment Honestly guys. I'd love to get all the feedback I can get. Also on the changelist, have started giving some lore examples for each caste, halfway done with examples for Paradox and have ported a Thaumaturgical ritual related to the Division of Endings. I hope everyone following this thread enjoys the new stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T23:13:34-07:00","id":1100724,"title":"","content":"I'm going to look over your Brawl Charms, since it doesn't look like anybody has so far. Let's get to it!<br /> <br /> Horrific Wreath: +2 damage and automatic Aggravated seems like a little much for an 1 mote charm. Ghost-Eating Technique costs 3m and also deals Aggravated against Spirits, but it's got some other effects too. I think this charm could do with having its cost raised to 2 or 3 motes, just to keep it balanced with other Withering damage-adders.<br /> <br /> Tolerant Strife: A little more broadly applicable than Dipping Swallow Defense, but also a mite more expensive. I think this charm is alright. 3 motes means that it's expensive to keep using when one is suffering from wound penalties or other debilitations, but it's still pretty strong.<br /> <br /> Fateful Feint: This one is pretty unique and fascinating. Recouping the motes spent on an attack is pretty useful, and the automatic success is a nice reward. I think something like this might be a bit too all around useful. Maybe it could have a minor Initiative cost and the Perilous tag? The Willpower cost might be enough, but it can easily be regained through stunting or other means.<br /> <br /> Shooting Star Suplex: Perfect, I love it already.<br /> <br /> Wait, I need to mention the mechanics, don't I? So, it's 3 motes for a decisive counterattack that takes the form of a grapple gambit followed up by an immediate Slam. That's pretty hardcore. This is a fascinating counterattack Charm, very different from Solar Counterattack or Cross-Counter. I think it's alight as is. It resets the Sidereal to base Initiative, right?<br /> <br /> Judicious Use of Leverage: This is a pretty interesting mishmash of mechanics, allowing waifish little Sidereals to toss around big guys and then later huge monsters. The Essence 3 Repurchase seems on par with Titan-Straightening Method. I feel the 'must have a lower Strength than your opponent to sub in Wits' might be more trouble than it's worth, but I don't know enough to be sure.<br /> <br /> Ripples in Force: This charm has some badass imagery, but it's a little bit unclear. Mentioning Aim actions paints this as changing the way the attack works. It's still a melee Withering attack, right? Does it use its normal accuracy, or does it recalculate based on the distance between the Sidereal and their target?<br /> <br /> Unobstructed Blow: This as interesting armor-piercing attack, with some unique rules that set it apart from other similar charms. I like it.<br /> <br /> Broken Wing Atemi: Breaking limbs is awesome. This charm is great.<br /> <br /> Crimson Palm Counterstrike: So, it's just a reflexive decisive clash with some extra damage? I feel like this charm could use some extra bells and whistles, but the cost seems pretty in line with other counterattack charms.<br /> <br /> Mutually Dissatisfactory Compromise: So, a clash enhancer that basically means that both attacks hit and deal damage simultaneously. I don't think DV is the right terminology here. Defense seems to be what the book uses when it's talking about Evasion and Parry simultaneously.<br /> <br /> Flexible Fate Reversal: Oooh, a charm that lets you gain more control rounds mid-grapple. That Initiative cost makes this thing kinda risky, though. This charm seems interesting, especially with its multiple uses.<br /> <br /> Beatstick Encouragement: This charm's name doesn't really jive with me, but I love the effects. The 'damned if you do, damned if you don't' nature of the Intimidate action seems fun to play with. I'm unsure of how someone might react when faced with this charm, though. It's similar to other followup or secondary attack charms, but it seems a bit more broadly applicable. One Weapon,<br /> <br /> Two Blows has very stringed activation requirements, but I think the Willpower and the fact that the Intimidate has to be successful offset this.<br /> <br /> Forcing Hand Incantation: Yeeeeeee, prayer-strip charm! Hot damn, light artifact fists is a huge upgrade! That last sentence, though, that's absolute madness in a can. Double raw damage, or reroll failed dice on the attack roll? That's an absolutely brutal effect. I like it. This definitely seems like a great capstone, not to mention a great way of capturing how RIDICULOUS some Sidereal charms are meant to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T13:10:49-07:00","id":1100929,"title":"","content":"Hey I'm really glad to hear your input and have a few responses.<ul><li>Going to definitely take your advice over Horrific Wreath and Fateful Feint</li> <li>Shooting Star Suplex does reset you to base initiative. It follows the same rule as a normal Decisve Slam/Throw including adding your rounds of control to your damage and ending the grapple with your target prone.</li> <li>Ripples in Force has almost the same text as the Solar Charm Iron Raptor Technique, barring its unique capability to ignore cover. The Aiming thing is just a fact that all ranged attacks made at medium range or longer need an aim action before them unless otherwise said.</li> <li>Crimson Palm Counterstrike is kind of boring, especially compared to all the rest, but in first edition, Crimson Palm Counterstrike was a clash charms before clashes existed. I figured leaving it as a sort of bland clash charm would be a nice way to hearken back to its original incarnation. Adding bonus successes to damage (Albeit a limited amount) hearkened back to 1e and 2es way of dealing damage.</li> </ul><br /> All in all I'm really excited to see you like what I've written. Love to hear every bit of criticism, advice and general interest this project has","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T16:27:53-07:00","id":1111058,"title":"","content":"Finished a few new abilities. Updated the document for readability","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T22:22:23-07:00","id":1112511,"title":"","content":"Added Heart's Fire Style and Border of Kaleidoscopic Logic Style. The first is a martial art based on fiery emotions and friendship burning through the opposition; the second a Sidereal Martial art that destroys the target's perception of self","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T02:00:21-07:00","id":1112565,"title":"","content":"Reading your Martial Arts, which I find pretty cool, I have some doubts with your formatting<br /> <br /> Fists-as-Heart Understanding adds your intimacy level as damage... Damage what? Damage dice?Damage levels, ie, automatic successes? I guess they are dice, but maybe you should specify it. There is the same problem in Incendiary Acceleration Method, when it says you add your Intimacy level to the roll, but maybe you should specify &quot;Your intimacy level in dice (or noncharm dice) to the roll&quot;. Also, HeartfeltVow Empowerment. The added damage is suppossed to be extra dice, right, not direct damage/automatic successes, right?<br /> <br /> Smoldering Passion Emanation adds your Presence/2 or Martial Arts/2 to some rolls... What is the rounding? I mean, If I have 3 Presence, so 1\u00b45 after dividing, do I round down and add 1 dice, or up and add 2 dice?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Heart\u00b4s Fire is a cool style, and although I think it looks a bit in the weak side, it sounds fun to play with. With so many charms based upon the power in friendship, and the energy beams aesthethics, it is obligatory in any Shonen-inspired campaign XD<br /> <br /> Border of Kaleidoscopic Logic looks awesome, but I\u00b4m a sucker for Sidereals, mind-fuckery and weird, esoteric charms and martial arts, so the style was basically designed for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:36:40-07:00","id":1112698,"title":"","content":"Ah yeah. All of those should be dice, and by default round up thought I should note that in the document","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"htt